OL,3,GNEWSAWomen guilty of running illegal
OL,4,A28-pupil school
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo women have been convicted of
OL,7,Frunning an illegal school for 28 pupils
OL,8,Fin Birmingham after the operation was
OL,9,Finvestigated by Ofsted.
OL,11,FNoor Laiba Imani, 34, from Oldbury, and
OL,12,FMaryam Bi, 34, from Smethwick, were
OL,13,Ffound guilty of conducting an
OL,14,Funregistered independent educational
OL,15,Finstitution at Birmingham Magistrates'
OL,16,FCourt on Tuesday.
OL,18,FThe pair ran Bright Sparks Home
OL,19,FSchooling Ltd (BSHS) on Whitmore Road,
OL,20,Fwhich investigators found had an
OL,21,FIslamic faith ethos and was advertised
OL,22,Fas providing home schooling services.
OL,23,APub: 25-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
